{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1345296-fame-edge","id":1345296,"title":"Fame Edge","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-01T12:23:19-07:00","id":1345296,"title":"Fame Edge","content":"So it states that those who have the Fame Edge cannot have the Covert Edge or the Anonymous Enhanced Edge (and other such things) but I was wondering about opening this up based on location. Example, Person A is famous in Location C but is not known in Location A. Couldn't he make is to the Fame Edge applies to Location C but the Covert or Alternate Identity or whatnot Edge applies to anywhere else. <br /> <br /> Story examples. <br /> <br /> Stargate. SG-1 are Famous within both the SGC and the wider galaxy due to their exploits. BUT on Earth itself they are relatively unknown. So Fame would apply to their SGC and galacitc operations but their Alternate identity and Covert Edges could be applied on Earth. (Yes, this is indicating that enough 'action' takes place on Earth that such a purchase makes sense.) <br /> <br /> Aeon. Person A is a Nova on Eden, and thus has Fame, but he is unknown on Earth, and means to keep it that way, so when he teleports/warps to Earth he uses as much as he can to keep his nature secret, hence his Alternate Identity and Covert status. <br /> <br /> Just a thought I had as I am reading through the actual physical book. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T12:56:57-07:00","id":1345312,"title":"","content":"Fame is stated as focused on a subculture or local. And 3 dots is world wide, so if you have multiple worlds you may need more dots in fame to cover it. It probably could work as you say, I would state that to have covert or even treat other world entirely as a secret ID<br /> <br /> I would say, a planet like Eden, 1 dot is all you need to cover the entire planet.<br /> <br /> In the SG-1 it\u2019s about a subculture, the people that deal with StarGates, even among other worlds, SG1 specifically would be a Fame 3 focused on the STarGate users in general, while SG5 (I don\u2019t recall the numbers exactly) would have Fame 1, working on their field of specialisation (let\u2019s say relic hunters)<br /> <br /> Edit: Thinking a bit more, covert may be in part training on how to stay under radar and avoiding unnecessary identification. If you go that way, Covert and Secret Identity are more about skill while Fame is situational. You may be famous in on place and not in other, but being unknown and having the Covert edge are different things.<br /> <br /> SG1 may have covert and be famous among the people they interact but now the entire galaxy. They came from different arenas (even planets), so they would be known by more people than a group that came from the same neighbourhood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"http